adr: 0344
file: selfhost/apfront.pas
kills: badsema-traits
why: The refusal removed, so `trait Ordered` is declared and implemented and the program is told at the *call* that its own type is not admitted by a category it never wrote. AP 6.7.3.10.5 identifies the four spellings in a bound position by spelling alone and a bound is the only position a trait may stand in, so such a trait can never be applied.
--- old
  if CatOfName(d^.trAt, d^.trLen) <> tcNone then begin
    ErrorAt(d^.trNameLine, d^.trNameCol);
    write('a trait may not be named ''');
    WritePool(d^.trAt, d^.trLen);
    write(''': that spelling names a type-parameter category wherever a ');
    writeln('bound is written, so nothing could name this trait')
  end;
--- new
